---
title: "3 · Set up sections and tasks"
description: Add internal and client sections, add tasks, and set who does each task and when it is due.
sidebar:
  order: 4
  label: "3 · Set up sections and tasks"
---

**Who:** tenant admin. **Where:** the template editor, **Tasks** tab.

A section is one stage of the case. A task is one thing that someone does in that stage. When you add a section or a task, its settings panel opens automatically.

## The section menu

The **⋯** menu of a section contains **Section settings**, **Add task**, **Move up**, **Move down** and **Delete section**.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/section-menu" caption="The section menu." /%}

## An internal section

Open **Section settings** and set the section up:

{% steps %}

1. In **Name**, enter the section name, for example `Information collection`.
2. Under **Board status**, choose **Prep**. This is the column of the **Cases** board that the case is in while this section is open.
3. In **Sub-line on the card**, enter a short line to show on the case card.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/section-internal" caption="Section settings of an internal section." /%}

## A task

Select a task row to open its settings:

- **Name** and **What to do**.
- **Responsible**: **Our team**, **The client** or **ACRA**.
- The due date. In this example the task is due 2 business days after the case starts (**Counted from** **The case start date**, **Business days** `2`).

{% screenshot id="case-templates/task-settings" caption="The settings of a task." /%}

## Due after another task

To make a task due after another task:

{% steps %}

1. In **Counted from**, choose **Another task**.
2. In **Which task**, choose the task that it follows.
3. In **Business days**, enter the number of business days, for example `1`.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
Do not choose the task itself in **Which task**. A task cannot be due relative to itself, or to a task that is due relative to it.
{% /aside %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/task-due-after-task" caption="A task that is due 1 business day after another task." /%}

## A section that runs alongside the others

For a section such as `Invoice & payment`, open **Section settings** and, under **Behaviour**:

- Turn off **Moves the case forward**.
- Turn on **Runs in parallel**.

The section then does not hold up the sections after it, and it does not change the case's column on the board.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/section-parallel" caption="A section that runs in parallel." /%}

## Task options

- A task can be due on the case due date: in **Counted from**, choose **The case due date**.
- For work that is done in another system, turn on **Done outside StaffOnAI** under **Options**. The task row then shows the **Off-platform** label.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/task-options" caption="Task options, with Done outside StaffOnAI turned on." /%}

## A client section

Select **+ Add client section**, and then set the section up:

{% steps %}

1. Under **Chasing the client**, set the reminders, for example **Remind before it’s due** `2 days before due`, **Keep reminding** `Every 3 days`, and turn on **Remind again once overdue**.
2. Under **Board status**, choose **Waiting for client**.
3. In **Waiting on**, choose **The client**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/section-client" caption="Section settings of a client section." /%}

## A client task

Select **Add client task** in the client section, and name the task, for example `Sign engagement letter`.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/client-task" caption="A task in a client section." /%}
